NAME
       dhcpc - DHCP client for one interface

SYNOPSIS
       **dhcpc** __INTERFACE__

DESCRIPTION
       Gets an IPv4 address, netmask, gateway and DNS servers for
       __INTERFACE__ from a DHCP server (RFC 2131) and applies them. Listens on
       UDP port 68 (bootpc) and talks to servers on port 67 (bootps).

       Cycle: DISCOVER, OFFER, REQUEST, ACK. The lease is renewed at T1 (half
       of the lease by default) with a unicast REQUEST to the server and
       rebound at T2 (7/8 of the lease) with a broadcast. When the lease
       expires or the server answers NAK, the address is removed and the
       cycle starts again. The current lease is written to
       /run/dhcp/__INTERFACE__.lease.

       Normally started by netd(8). Needs root or the NET_ADMIN capability.

SIGNALS
       **SIGTERM** sends RELEASE to the server and removes the address.

SEE ALSO
       netd(8), ip(8)
